            <abstract>
                <p>According to <bibl><ptr target="bm:Lusini2002Pistoia"/><citedRange unit="page">172</citedRange></bibl>, 
                    a ‘Apocalisse di Esdra, sulla domenica’ (engl.: "Apocalypse of Ezra, on Sunday"), but according to 
                    <bibl><ptr target="bm:canamei"/></bibl>, a ‘Discourse delivered by the Lord on wisdom and the 
                    mysteries of holiness and the secrets of the Lord, to the prophet and sage Ezra’, but according to 
                    <bibl><ptr target="bm:EMML3"/><citedRange unit="page">445</citedRange></bibl>, it is a ‘Revelation of Ezra the Scribe
                    on the observance of Sunday’. As it is noted in the text, this work was translated by 
                    <persName ref="PRS15565JacobJer">‘Jacob of Jerusalem’</persName>.</p>
            </abstract>
